{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Incident record — blast radius (AC8)\n\n**What happened.** 2026-08-03 19:13, a session posted a comment on ticket 129e whose body\nwas a full zsh environment dump. The dump embedded SEVEN live credentials: Anthropic, two\nGitHub PATs, Gemini/Google, Jira/Atlassian, an OpenAI service-account key, and a PyPI token.\n\n**Mechanism.** The body was produced by an unquoted shell command substitution. The shell\nexpanded it before rebar saw anything, so rebar received an ordinary string and — having no\nwrite-time screen at `append_event` — wrote it. The store auto-pushes, so the comment was\npublished on the next push attempt.\n\n**Blast radius.** GitHub push protection rejected `refs/heads/tickets` (GH013) on the\nAnthropic key. Because rebar's tickets branch is a single shared ref, EVERY session's store\nwrites then queued local-only — 153 commits at diagnosis. This was a full store-sharing\noutage for all concurrent agents, caused by one comment, and it presented as transient\ncontention rather than as a leak: the only symptom was\n`WARNING rebar._store.push: tickets branch push failed after 3 retries`.\n\n**The control that actually stopped the leak was OUTSIDE this project.** Nothing in rebar\ndetected, refused, or reported the credentials. GitHub push protection did — and it did so\nby breaking the store for everyone, which is the loudest possible failure mode and the least\nuseful one. That is the gap this ticket closes: the same refusal, moved to the write seam,\nwhere it costs one command instead of the whole branch.\n\n**Secondary defect, already fixed elsewhere.** The push-retry path swallowed the git stderr,\nso the outage did not self-identify. That was bug 2a76 (`test_push_rejection_surfacing.py`),\nwhich landed the GH013 reason + unpushed backlog into the warning. AC3 and its half of AC4\nare therefore already satisfied on main; this change does not duplicate them."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786099291319170001,"uuid":"9e2f52b0-8c8d-4653-805d-46ef74de1655"}